{"id":"be1aeaae-f19f-4d82-a4ff-7831961b22f1","createdAt":"2026-10-26T13:57:26.322Z","batchId":"states_claude-sonnet-5-5_low","approach":"html","modelId":"claude-sonnet-5-5","settings":{"effort":"low"},"presetId":"states","prompt":"Two states for a file list: an empty state with an upload call to action, and an error state with a retry button.","system":"Return only the body content of an HTML page: no doctype, <html>, <head> or <body> tags, no markdown, no code fences, no prose. The page shell below is already loaded, so build with its classes and chart helper. Inline <script> is allowed for interactivity (tabs, toggles, filters); no external requests. Add a small <style> block only for what the classes cannot express, or when the request asks for a different look, colours, fonts or layout: then follow the request.\nPAGE SHELL (already loaded; do not restate it):\n- A stylesheet with these classes. Use them instead of writing CSS:\n  layout: page (centered column), stack, row, between, center, gap-sm, gap-lg, grid + cols-2|cols-3|cols-4 (responsive)\n  surfaces: card, card-title, card-desc, alert, alert-destructive, hr\n  text: h1-h4 (styled), lead, muted, small, up, down (trend colours)\n  controls: btn, btn-secondary|btn-outline|btn-ghost|btn-destructive, btn-sm|btn-lg, btn-block; label wraps input/select/textarea; label.check wraps a checkbox or radio\n  data: table (styled; td.num for numbers), badge, badge-secondary|badge-outline|badge-destructive, stat-label, stat-value, progress (inner div with style=\"width:NN%\"), avatar\n- Charts: <div data-chart='{\"type\":\"bar|line|area|pie\",\"title\":\"…\",\"data\":[{\"label\":\"W1\",\"value\":120}]}'></div> renders an SVG chart (single series, pie gets a legend). Do not draw charts yourself.\n- Light and dark mode are handled by the stylesheet.\n\nDESIGN BRIEF (applies to every UI you produce):\n- Build a complete, realistic screen, not a skeleton: a clear title and intro, grouped sections, and enough detail that it could ship.\n- Cover exactly what the request names, with no extra pages or marketing sections.\n- Use the supplied DATA in full: every field is there to be shown. Derive useful extras from it (shares, totals, deltas, rankings) instead of inventing unrelated numbers.\n- Where it fits, add status badges, trend/change figures, secondary actions, helper text, and sensible empty or edge-case copy.\n- Establish hierarchy with headings, size and weight; group related items; keep spacing and alignment consistent.\n- Make charts readable: a title, labelled axes or values, and a legend for pie charts.\n- Never use lorem ipsum or placeholder names like \"Item 1\".","systemHash":"0c16911c9564c3db3ada7a622931ee6ffc820ebf9a373996782a9f1f0fc3c98c","systemOverridden":false,"strictOutput":false,"rawOutput":"<div class=\"page stack gap-lg\">\n  <div class=\"stack\">\n    <h1>Project files</h1>\n    <p class=\"lead\">Preview how the file list looks when there is nothing to show and when loading fails. Switch between the two states below.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"row gap-sm\">\n    <button class=\"btn\" id=\"tab-empty\" type=\"button\">Empty state</button>\n    <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" id=\"tab-error\" type=\"button\">Error state</button>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card stack\" id=\"panel-empty\">\n    <div class=\"between\">\n      <div>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">Q3 Brand Launch</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">0 files · 0 B of 5 GB used</div>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"badge badge-secondary\">Empty</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"progress\"><div style=\"width:0%\"></div></div>\n    <table class=\"table\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Modified</th><th>Owner</th><th class=\"num\">Size</th></tr></thead>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"stack center\" style=\"text-align:center;padding:2.5rem 1rem;border:2px dashed var(--border, #8884);border-radius:12px\" id=\"drop\">\n      <div style=\"font-size:2.5rem\" aria-hidden=\"true\">📁</div>\n      <h3>No files yet</h3>\n      <p class=\"muted\">Upload designs, contracts or spreadsheets to share them with your team.<br>Drag and drop files here, or browse from your computer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row gap-sm center\">\n        <label class=\"btn btn-lg\" style=\"cursor:pointer\">Upload files<input type=\"file\" multiple hidden id=\"file\"></label>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-lg\" type=\"button\">Import from Drive</button>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"small muted\">Max 500 MB per file · PDF, PNG, JPG, DOCX, XLSX, ZIP</p>\n      <p class=\"small\" id=\"picked\"></p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card stack\" id=\"panel-error\" hidden>\n    <div class=\"between\">\n      <div>\n        <div class=\"card-title\">Q3 Brand Launch</div>\n        <div class=\"card-desc\">File list unavailable</div>\n      </div>\n      <span class=\"badge badge-destructive\">Error</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"alert alert-destructive\">\n      <strong>We couldn't load your files.</strong>\n      <div class=\"small\">The server didn't respond (error 503). Your files are safe, and nothing has been deleted.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stack center\" style=\"text-align:center;padding:2rem 1rem\">\n      <div style=\"font-size:2.5rem\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⚠️</div>\n      <h3>Something went wrong</h3>\n      <p class=\"muted\">Check your connection and try again. If the problem continues, contact support with the reference below.</p>\n      <div class=\"row gap-sm center\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-lg\" id=\"retry\" type=\"button\">Retry</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-lg\" type=\"button\">Contact support</button>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"small muted\" id=\"status\">Reference: ERR-503-FL · Last attempt just now</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\nconst e=document.getElementById('panel-empty'),r=document.getElementById('panel-error');\nconst te=document.getElementById('tab-empty'),tr=document.ge